{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793552972,"nonce":"kTOCUlleLS1ru4eqhhScc08Qe08=","title":"Headless Ashui preview: Linux hosts, regression check and open gaps","message":"Preview App on an Ashui hl project now runs the app headless in the workspace session and streams surface records (shims/ashui/ashui/app/WindowedApp.hx, scripts/ashui-surface.sh), replacing the wasm build. Pointer, wheel, typed text, editing/arrow/navigation/letter/digit keys, resize and the viewer's pixel ratio work; verified only in headless Chrome against small apps and the landing page demo on a Mac.\n\nOpen:\n- Linux hosts: Offscreen.create() needs a wgpu adapter (Vulkan or GL) and asks for the high-performance adapter without a fallback; a software driver such as Mesa lavapipe should satisfy it but nobody has tried. Ashui's own render lanes run only on macOS and a NUC. A sandboxed runner has to provide one.\n- Natives: the script copies blinc_abi, xgpu and xwindow hdlls from RayDE's bin; the real runner's toolchain image needs them and the script on its PATH/env (RAYDE_ASHUI_SURFACE).\n- No repeatable check: a regression test should build a small app through the script, read the first surface frame, click a button and see the counter change, and type then backspace in an input. Today this was done by hand with puppeteer.\n- Fidelity against the windowed renderer is not compared pixel for pixel. Media (ashui.media), clipboard, cursor and menus do nothing offscreen.\n- Every frame is a full readback; no damage rectangles.\n- Moving the window to a display with another pixel ratio needs a restart of the preview.\n- Keys other than the mapped set are ignored.","files":null}]}